eep C, or argue otherwise. We need to consider missing criteria: we still lack decision quality for B, crew cooperation for D, etc. But we have enough to decide? The panel hasn't covered all criteria fully. However we can still argue.\n\nWe have evidence: C keeps calm in crisis (stress resilience), 100% reliability, quick correct decisions, positive crew atmosphere, excellent attention skills, puts concern for others above everything. Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nB: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, pretentious, wrong tone, makes nasty remarks. So B's crew cooperation is poor.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentration, solves problems, takes responsibility seriously, moody, loner. No stress resilience explicit, but \"responds to unexpected events adequately\" maybe indicates some resilience. No crew cooperation examples.\n\nA: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, leadership, unfriendly, eats unhealthily, not good at criticism, unorganized. No stress resilience.\n\nThus C seems best overall. So Agent 3 should likely keep vote for C, referencing Agent 2's argument and adding maybe additional evidence about C's crew atmosphere and reliability, and note that B's crew cooperation issues are more severe. Also note that C's communication difficulty is a concern but can be mitigated with training.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: I agree with Agent 2, keep C. Provide evidence: stress resilience (keeps calm in crisis), reliability, quick decisions, positive crew atmosphere, attention skills, concern for others. Compare to B's nasty remarks. Conclude vote for C.\n\nMETADATA_JSON: vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
